# Static dashboard deploy: ship only what the browser needs.
# NOTE: real-cfd-patients.json MUST ship — app.js fetches it at runtime for the
# computed CFD cases. Do not add *.json here.

# source / tooling that never reaches the browser
# NOTE: services/ IS shipped — api/index.py imports services/api/main.py
# for the serverless function. Only the worker subtree is excluded.
neuroflow-local-pipeline
packages
infra
node_modules
.venv
__pycache__
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
package.json

# documents
docs
*.dcm
# ...but the three sample scans MUST ship. They are what the Upload DICOM / MRA
# control is demonstrated with, and each is genuine DICOM (~14 KB) matching a
# case that has a completed CFD run, so uploading one shows real computed
# hemodynamics rather than a placeholder.
!samples/*.dcm
*.pdf
*.docx
*.md
python-script.txt

# local state
.wrangler
.supabase
.env
.env.*
services/worker

# Retired: 35.7 MB generic nerve asset, ~70 s to download, unrelated to any
# patient's vasculature. Replaced by per-case models/{id}.glb (~1 MB) exported
# from the actual solved surface. Kept in git history, not shipped.
NervesOnly_v1.glb

# Local test scans for exercising the upload control. Deliberately NOT
# served: they exist to be uploaded BY a user, so they must not already
# be sitting on the site.
test-uploads
